  "reasoning": "Russia imposed the food embargo in August 2014 [1] and extended it for another year in early August 2015 [2], while simultaneously expanding the list of embargoed nations to include Iceland, Albania, Montenegro, and Liechtenstein [3]. The extension in August 2015 was explicitly for a full year, meaning the embargo was set to remain in place until at least August 2016. As of the latest available information in September 2015, there was no indication of a partial or full lift of the embargo before the August 6, 2016 deadline [4]. Given the explicit one-year extension and the lack of any announced policy reversal, it is highly unlikely that Russia would lift any part of the embargo before the specified date.",
