      "fact": "In late January 2017, the VIX spiked by more than 50% due to geopolitical jitters regarding the Korean peninsula, reaching a peak of approximately 17.5.",
      "source_date": "2017-01-27"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "fact": "Historically, the VIX Index typically trades between 12 and 20, with values above 25 occurring only during significant market turmoil or crises.",
      "source_date": "2016-12-31"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "fact": "As of the knowledge cutoff date of September 14, 2017, there were no public records of the VIX Index exceeding 25 in the first nine months of 2017.",
      "source_date": "2017-09-14"
    }
  ],
  "reasoning": "The VIX Index was trading near record lows (below 11) at the start of 2017 [1] and remained in a low-volatility regime throughout the first half of the year [2]. Although a geopolitical event in late January 2017 caused a spike of over 50%, the index only reached approximately 17.5, well below the 25 threshold [3]. Historical context indicates that values above 25 are rare and typically associated with severe market crises, which were not present in the 2017 market environment prior to October [4]. Furthermore, data available up to the knowledge cutoff of September 14, 2017, confirms that the VIX had not breached 25 during the first nine months of 2017 [5]. Given the absence of a major market crash or significant turmoil in the months leading up to October 2017, it is highly unlikely the index would spike above 25 in the short window remaining before October 15.",
  "probability_yes": 0.05,
  "prediction": "no"
}

